    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "66fab0ce-517c-52bc-b5fd-b725eb76bef6",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-3 \\\\ -2x-6y &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=1,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
